<title>USA: Meredith completes TV station purchases.</title>
<headline>Meredith completes TV station purchases.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Meredith Corp, a publishing and broadcasting company, said Tuesday it has completed the purchase of three television stations from First Media Television LP for a total of $216 million.</p>
<p>The stations are KPDX-TV, serving Portland, Ore.; KFXO-TV, serving Bend, Ore.; and WHNS-TV, serving Asheville, N.C., and Greenville, S.C..  All three station are affiliates of News Corp Ltd's Fox network.</p>
<p>Meredith's broadcast group now includes 10 television stations, the company said.</p>
<p>Meredith shares were up 1/2 at 29-1/2 Tuesday.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
</text>
